PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Split between two interpretations: (A) 8-bit quantization only (multiples of 1/255) excludes exactly the two options containing 0.5 → answer 3,4 (Colleagues 1,4,6,8); (B) ROMM→sRGB gamut mapping (ProPhoto primaries + D50, matrix to D65 sRGB) produces negative channel(s) for the wide-gamut primaries and some mixtures → answer 1,2 or 1,2,3 (Colleagues 2,3,5,7).  
Key evidence preserved: ROMM(0,0,1) and ROMM(0,1,0) lie on the ProPhoto blue/green primaries far outside Rec.709; (0,0.5,0.6) is a high-chroma green–blue edge mixture that still yields ≥1 negative sRGB coordinate after conversion; (0.4,0.5,0.6) and (1,1,1) land inside [0,1]^3.  
Why ROMM is mentioned at all strongly favors gamut reading over pure numeric encoding; therefore current belief tilts to 1,2,3. Unresolved: exact floating-point result of the ROMM-to-sRGB matrix for option 3. No change yet from round-0 data.}

